# TraceGrid — Bob AI Coding Rules

## 1. Schema-First Development
- **Never** write a DB migration, model, or API handler before the `architecture.md` `## Database Schema` section is committed.
- **Never** add a new API endpoint without a corresponding row in the `## API Routes` table.
- **Never** create a new frontend component that calls an API without a matching entry in `## Request Flows`.
- When in doubt, update `architecture.md` first, then write code.

## 2. AST & Scanning Rules
- The scanner (`packages/core/src/scanner.ts`) must operate on **file contents only** — no spawning subprocesses, no importing project code at runtime.
- Each scanner sub-function must be a **pure function**: `(content: string, filePath: string) => ScanResult`.
- Regex patterns used for scanning must be **named and documented** with an inline comment explaining what they match and why.
- The scanner must **never throw** on unrecognised file formats — return an empty result instead.

## 3. Parser Strictness
- The parser (`packages/core/src/parser.ts`) must be **deterministic**: same input → same output, always.
- Sections in `architecture.md` are identified by **exact heading text** (case-sensitive). Do not use fuzzy matching.
- Mermaid blocks are extracted between ` ```mermaid ` and ` ``` ` delimiters only. Do not attempt to parse inline Mermaid.
- If a required section is missing, the parser must throw a descriptive `ParseError` — not silently return partial data.

## 4. Type Safety
- All public functions in `packages/core` must have **explicit TypeScript return types**.
- No `any` types in `packages/core/src/types.ts` or `packages/core/src/parser.ts`.
- Use `unknown` with a type guard instead of casting with `as`.
- Interfaces are preferred over `type` aliases for object shapes.

## 5. Code Modularity
- Each file in `packages/core/src/` has **one responsibility**. Do not add parser logic to `scanner.ts` or vice versa.
- Exports from `packages/core` flow through `src/index.ts` only. No deep imports (`packages/core/src/parser`) from outside the package.
- The CLI (`packages/cli`) depends on `packages/core` via its public API only.

## 6. Error Handling
- Use typed error classes (`class ParseError extends Error`, `class ScanError extends Error`).
- Never swallow errors silently. Log with context (`file`, `line`, `section`) before re-throwing or returning.
- CLI commands must exit with code `1` on error and print a human-readable message to stderr.

## 7. File Generation
- The generator (`packages/core/src/generator.ts`) must produce output that the parser can round-trip without loss.
- Use template literals with explicit section headings — no string concatenation of partial sections.
- Generated `architecture.md` must always include all four required sections (even if empty tables/blocks).

## 8. Testing Expectations
- New scanner sub-functions must have at least one unit test with a synthetic input string.
- Parser tests must include a valid full `architecture.md` fixture and at least one error-path case.
- Tests live in `packages/core/src/__tests__/` and use the project's test runner.

## 9. Dependency Policy
- `packages/core`: **zero** runtime npm dependencies. Only `devDependencies` for TypeScript/testing.
- `packages/cli`: only `commander`, `express`, and `@types/*` are permitted.
- Do not introduce additional dependencies without explicit approval.

## 10. Commit Hygiene
- Each commit must touch either `architecture.md` OR code files — not both in the same commit.
- Commit messages follow: `type(scope): short description` (e.g. `feat(scanner): add Prisma model extractor`).
